  <content>
  <section><title>Activity </title>
<para><figure><media alt="Three steps of a growing pattern."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/a565fecb7bfa3dc272c528be5f11d1b7e33a45f0"/></media></figure></para>
<para>Here is a pattern of squares.</para>
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Is the number of small squares growing linearly? Explain how you know.</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>No, there are 3 squares in the first step, 6 squares in the second step, and 11 squares in the third step. So the
      number of additional squares is 3 going from the first to the second step and 5 going from the second to the third
      step.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>Answer questions a–e to complete the table.</item>
</list>
<table class="os-raise-midsizetable">
  <thead>
    <row>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">
        Step
      </entry>
